      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The FeNiCrMn alloy has a low stacking-fault energy of approximately 20 mJ/m².",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::chunk::002::discussion::aad813a188"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial material contains no pre-existing BCC phase.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::chunk::002::discussion::aad813a188"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yielding begins through nucleation of partial dislocations.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The yield-initiating partial dislocations nucleate at surface defects.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial-dislocation nucleation at yielding is thermally activated.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial-dislocation nucleation produces stacking faults, which are followed by deformation twinning and HCP martensitic transformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2",
        "PMC5461481::chunk::002::discussion::aad813a188"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accumulation of dislocations and stacking faults promotes transformation to HCP.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain boundaries are dislocation-nucleation sites in polycrystalline analogs.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dominant post-yield deformation mode involves TWIP together with HCP martensitic transformation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "FCC-to-BCC transformation is not the primary deformation mode.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2",
        "PMC5461481::chunk::002::discussion::aad813a188"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The anomalously low strain-rate sensitivity may arise from high activation-energy barriers for dislocation motion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yield strength will have minimal dependence on strain rate over 10⁻⁴ to 10² s⁻¹.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yield strength will depend strongly on temperature between 77 K and 600 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HCP phase fraction will increase with increasing tensile strain and decreasing temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::002::results_and_discussion::b39f44a3e2",
        "PMC5461481::chunk::002::discussion::aad813a188"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "BCC phase will remain absent during tensile loading.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
